<title>BRAZIL: Brazil cenbank sets new weaker trade level on real.</title>
<headline>Brazil cenbank sets new weaker trade level on real.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's Central Bank signalled a new weaker trading level for the real currency by buying dollars at 1.019 real and selling dollars at 1.024 real in a buy/sell tender in the commercial foreign exchange market, dealers said.</p>
<p>Under the previous mini-band set on Sept 10, the real was traded between 1.018 and 1.023 real to the dollar.</p>
<p>-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55-11-2324411.</p>
